  monica to change the directors across  the games we've had really good success  with that corey is the only repeat  director and rightfully so he's damn  good at what he does corey barlock added  the important thing for us is to be able  to get a fresh perspective each time but  also a fresh pair of legs in the sense  that you're really exhausted at the end  of finishing one of these things so  you've got to con somebody else into  doing it  now you are ready  [Music]  god of war ragnarok is planned for ps5  but it's also coming to ps4 the news of  a previous gen version was quietly  shared via a q a with hermann holst the  head of playstation studios at the  september playstation showcase sony  confirmed that ragnarok will be released  across ps5 and ps4 although there is no  word yet on any big differences between  the editions that might exist  and what about pc well this is all  speculative right now given sony's  recent track record of slowly bringing  some of its biggest playstation games to  pc it does make sense to question the  possibility for a pc version of god of  war ragnarok sony also recently acquired  the pc port specialist nix's software  fueling rumors that it might bring more  of its first-party games to pc to help  expand their audience while a pc edition  of ragnarok hasn't been confirmed yet  hulst mentioned in an interview on the  playstation blog that the company  continues to further invest in the pc  space but if it's anything like previous  sony releases on pc it's likely not to  come to the platform for some time if it  ever does  we'll let you know when we do  if you're interested in a  behind-the-scenes look at how the 2018  god of war was made check out our  episode of audio logs where game  director corey barlog breaks down one of  the most pivotal scenes how it was  created and the crucial gameplay  mechanic that was almost cut from the  game  and we really had to figure out how to  take the old moves and make them work  much bette